{"ref":"2018.MM38.14","summary":"Over the past few years, several Councillors have independently hired paper shredding companies to attend their local Environment Day. This allows residents to recycle papers that contain information too sensitive to dispose of during regular curbside recycling pickup. As an increased number of Councillors add this service to their Environment Day lineup, it is clear that a structured, City-wide process is needed.","decided":"City Council on March 26 and 27, 2018, adopted the following: 1. City Council direct the General Manager, Solid Waste Management Services, to report back to the Public Works and Infrastructure Committee in 2018 on the potential of adding paper shredding services to the 2019 Environment Day itinerary.","motions":[{"stage":"City Council","when":"","desc":"Two-Thirds required - MM38.14 - Waive referral","type":"Waive Referral","result":"Carried, 28-11","yes":28,"no":11,"votes":[["Anthony Perruzza","Yes"],["Cesar Palacio","Yes"],["Chin Lee","Yes"],["Christin Carmichael Greb","Yes"],["David Shiner","Yes"],["Frank Di Giorgio","Yes"],["Glenn De Baeremaeker","Yes"],["Gord Perks","Yes"],["Janet Davis","Yes"],["Jim Hart","Yes"],["Joe Cressy","Yes"],["Joe Mihevc","Yes"],["John Campbell","Yes"],["John Filion","Yes"],["Josh Matlow","Yes"],["Kristyn Wong-Tam","Yes"],["Lucy Troisi","Yes"],["Maria Augimeri","Yes"],["Mary Fragedakis","Yes"],["Mary-Margaret McMahon","Yes"],["Michelle Holland","Yes"],["Mike Layton","Yes"],["Neethan Shan","Yes"],["Norman Kelly","Yes"],["Paul Ainslie","Yes"],["Paula Fletcher","Yes"],["Shelley Carroll","Yes"],["Vincent Crisanti","Yes"],["Denzil Minnan-Wong","No"],["Frances Nunziata","No"],["James Pasternak","No"],["Jaye Robinson","No"],["Jon Burnside","No"],["Josh Colle","No"],["Justin J. Di Ciano","No"],["Mark Grimes","No"],["Michael Ford","No"],["Michael Thompson","No"],["Stephen Holyday","No"],["Ana Bailão","Absent"],["Gary Crawford","Absent"],["Giorgio Mammoliti","Absent"],["Jim Karygiannis","Abs